## 3. The Market Gap

* **Government Macro Portals ([FASAL](https://www.ncfc.gov.in/fasal.html), [YES-TECH](https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2297646&reg=48&lang=1), [Krishi-DSS](https://krishi-dss.gov.in/)):** Built for ministry crop-cutting experiments, food procurement, and PMFBY insurance payouts at district/Gram Panchayat levels. They do not give plot-specific "what-if" input timing optimization to farmers.
* **Commercial Enterprise & Hardware Startups ([Cropin](https://www.cropin.com/), [Fasal](https://www.fasal.co/)):** Cropin sells B2B SaaS to large agribusinesses; Fasal relies on on-farm IoT sensor poles (`Fasal Sense`) costing ₹15,000–₹50,000+, making it unaffordable for India's 86% smallholder farmers.
* **Reactive Advisory Apps ([Plantix](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026), [DeHaat](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026)):** Diagnose leaf diseases from smartphone photos *after* visible infection has occurred, without quantitative yield-vs-resource counterfactual modeling.

## 4. Recommended Winning Solution: **Pragnya KisanPulse**

**Pragnya KisanPulse** is an open-data, zero-hardware **Counterfactual Yield & Input-Timing Decision Engine** designed for smallholder farmers and Farmer Producer Organizations (FPOs):
1. **Zero-Friction Plot Onboarding:** Uses GPS coordinates or [AgriStack UFSI](https://creuto.com/agristack-api-ufsi-farmer-registry-agritech) / [Digital Crop Survey](https://tgdcs.agristack.gov.in/crop-survey-tg/) plot polygons plus [ISRIC SoilGrids](https://un-spider.org/sites/default/files/GeoAI%20Compendium%202026.pdf) and [Soil Health Card](https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2221117&reg=3&lang=1) district/village nutrient baselines.
2. **Cloud-Penetrating Satellite + Weather Fusion:** Combines **Sentinel-2** 10m optical bands (`SAVI` for early 81-day yield prediction, `NDMI` for root-zone moisture stress, `NDRE` for pre-visual nitrogen status) with **Sentinel-1 C-band SAR** backscatter (`VV/VH`) so monitoring never goes blind during monsoon clouds ([Copernicus Data Space](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/data-collections/copernicus-sentinel-missions/sentinel-1), [IJISAE Study](https://ijisae.org/index.php/IJISAE/article/view/2326)).
3. **Uncertainty-Aware Hybrid Yield Predictor:** Uses **CatBoost/XGBoost + Conformal Quantile Regression** to output a calibrated yield range (`P10 Downside`, `P50 Expected`, `P90 Upside` in quintals/acre) rather than an overconfident point estimate ([ResearchGate Oct 2026 Hybrid ML Study](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/417267952_Hybrid_Machine_Learning_Models_for_Agricultural_Yield_Prediction_Integrating_Satellite_Imagery_Weather_Data_and_Soil_Parameters_for_Indian_Crops)).
4. **Counterfactual Action Optimizer (The Core Innovation):** Simulates 7-day intervention options (*Irrigate Now vs. Delay 4 Days*, *Apply Full Urea Today vs. Split Dose Post-Rain*) against incoming rainfall and evapotranspiration, ranking actions by **Net Farmer Return (₹/acre saved + quintals protected)** and delivering a **15-second vernacular WhatsApp voice alert** in Telugu, Hindi, or Marathi.
